 /// `grid_groups` (1 .. cap_groups; 0 = cap_groups) groups run side by side, a block row each striding over the rest:
 /// a call that usually has few groups or none (the verify window's PCIe share) launches less for the ones it does
 /// not have.  The results do not depend on it.
+/// `max_group_entries`: optional caller-proven upper bound, 0 when unknown. EXP_MODE=10 takes
+/// its gfx1030 singleton specialization only for 1 and GU={18,21,22}, Down={20,42};
+/// unknown/larger bounds and other format pairs keep mode 9.
+/// This selects a performance variant only: kernels still iterate the device group bounds.
 void native_expert_grouped(const NativeExpertLayout& L, const unsigned long long* grp_ptr, const int32_t* grp_start,
